    "turn_text": "Well, I had to go back last week and I got to tell you, you know, it's interesting trying to fly. I was told there was an article in Sunday's paper saying that Dane County had a hundred people fly through the airport last week. And I actually drove to O'Hare. And even out of O'Hare, there was only two flights going to DC and they canceled one of them on Thursday. So I got out on Wednesday and I couldn't get home on Thursday because that's I got home on Friday. There were nine people on my plane. It's a different surreal experience right now, but I'll go back in about two weeks to DC. It looks like assuming they can get some things in place to make sure that our staff are safe and the public is safe and we are coming back.",
