  {
    "episode_id": 93205,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/9/3/93205.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 10,
    "turn_text": "Yeah, well, you know, first of all, I mean, in the state of Wisconsin, I fully support the governor's safer home efforts, you know, until we are medically able to reopen. And that's what the governor is waiting for. I think even the president's guidelines say 14 days of declining virus cases in your state is when you're safe. But even then, we've got to do a whole lot more increased testing, contact tracing, isolation for people who do have it in place to actually be able to reopen safely. So in Washington, we know Donald Trump has done a pathetic a job in dealing with COVID-19. I could talk for hours just on all the things the missteps he made. Before we came back about seven, eight weeks ago now from DC, I had regular meetings with Dr. Fauci, with the FDA Commissioner Han, with the NIH, with the CDC. Those were all through my subcommittees and appropriations. Back eight weeks ago, I believe it was, could even have been longer, Dr. Fauci said if we closed down the whole country, for just two weeks, we probably would have got through this. Well, we didn't do any of those things. And here we are now 50,000, 60,000",
