    "turn_text": "Yeah, so you know, I think the logical side of my argument would be we have to listen to medical professionals, right? If even the president who's not even following his own advice says you have to have 14 days of decline to be considered safe to reopen, no state right now is in that position, we at least should be following that, right? Because otherwise you're going to have another spike. Some of these states are going to guarantee Florida and Georgia and Texas are likely to have another spike. It's going to prolong the pain for all of us. But I understand I want to be able to see people again and do things. But I want to do it without making my neighbors and my family members and my customers and my constituents sick. because of it, right? And I think one thing I'd really say, you know, I understand some people who came to that rally last Friday did it out of fear. Some were politically manipulated because there was some political money trying to reinvent the tea party, you know, movement again. But I think a lot of people also would like to reopen, but we understand we can't yet, right? So we've got to wait until we get those numbers down, which should I think the peak is about seven to 10 days away still in Wisconsin. And then we should be on that decline. But that's when it's going to be safe. But there's not a lot of business right now anyway. I mean, I saw a survey, 80% of people said they wouldn't go to a restaurant right now if it was open. So",
