    "turn_text": "if you get your taxes taken out of your check, generally there's enough that you get a little refund. So I think some people might have did that free this really spiking, right? Because you got your W-2 at the end of January. For those of us who wait longer, you know, I just noticed I had to pay in a little bit to the state and federal. And they did just cash the checks. So at least they're processing things and they're doing that, but people have till mid-July. So for people who know, who might have now need the money for other things, that could be an impact. And we're going to have to look at how that's going to be. The good news is that we're trying to look at all sorts of issues. can't afford rent or mortgages in many cases right now. We can't have people being evicted, right? People can't pay their student loans back. So we've got a six month moratorium on that, including no accruing interest during that period. So we're trying to look at all those sorts of things because unfortunately, This isn't going to end real soon. Now, yesterday, there was some great news that came out though, Henry. I've been following Scott Gottlieb, who's the former FDA commissioner, the first one under Trump. So he works for a conservative think tank, and he's one of my go-to guys, because he's just a good a drug that he's been saying for a while. He thought would have some positive results. And just yesterday, they got their numbers back and Dr. Fauci talked about it. It shows that for people who are in higher risk areas, so if you're older or have any of the other conditions, heart disease, diabetes, et cetera. It shows if people get that early enough, about a 30% of reduction in time suffering from a disease. And towards the later part, usually that first week, you may not have as intense symptoms and it gets bad. And that's when people have had to be put on ventilators. So what we need are some of these therapies in place, especially by fall. We now have a promising drug. And based on that, probably we can look at a class of drugs. And then we're gonna figure out how the antibodies work. There also is some promising stuff happening, but we got to understand that for a couple months it's going to be most of May yet. before we actually get through this safely. And if we do that, we're going to have deep, deep depression-like conditions for a couple months. But because of it, we'll come out of it. And we've got all kinds of other things that are good on the horizon. But if we try to get back too quick, like Georgia and Florida and Texas, that's when you're likely to have another spike. And then what are you going to do? Close down all over again. That will kill. many restaurant owners, I know, many retail owners. Manufacturing is down right now in many areas. That would be the worst thing",
